Work of ours this repository builds on
--------------------------------------
- agentprivacy dual-agent harness — https://github.com/mitchuski/agentprivacy-harness
  (Apache-2.0). The two held-apart seats follow its method; lib/dcbor.mjs is its
  canonical-encoding module (tools/dcbor.mjs there), carried here unchanged.
- kappa-evidence-mage — https://github.com/mitchuski/kappa-evidence-mage (code Apache-2.0,
  documents CC BY 4.0).
  The evidence bundle layout (objects, blobs, edges, one root) follows its ledgers, and the
  second verifier, tools/verify_py.py, imports its kappa.py at run time; no copy is vendored.

Open-source software used
-------------------------
- near-sdk-rs 5.29 (MIT OR Apache-2.0) — the gate and registry contracts.
- near-api-js 7 (MIT AND Apache-2.0) — chain calls from the seats and tools.
- @noble/post-quantum 0.7, with @noble/hashes and @noble/curves (MIT, Paul Miller) —
  ML-DSA-65 (FIPS 204) and SLH-DSA-SHA2-128s (FIPS 205).
- Node.js built-ins (node:crypto, node:test) — ed25519, SHA-256, SHA3-256, the test runner.
- The full dependency tree and its licences are in package-lock.json and the two Cargo.lock files.

Specifications followed
-----------------------
- Deterministic CBOR (dCBOR), draft-mcnally-deterministic-cbor — canonical encoding of every object.
- IETF LAMPS composite signature drafts — the shape of the hybrid signing message.
- NEP-297 — contract events.

Services
--------
- NEAR AI Cloud — private inference for both seats; its signature and attestation endpoints
  are consumed, not modified. Deeper TDX and NVIDIA checks are left to nearai-cloud-verifier.
- NEAR testnet — the gates pause.caesura.testnet and gap.caesura.testnet, and the registry.

